Quartic graphs with few pentagons through each edge
===================================================

The complete proof recovers three prior lower-bound clauses from fixed source F012, Table 2, physical page 18. It gives no whole-original, upper-bound, exact-count, question, Lean or measurement credit.

Run ``python check.py --study STUDY --out NEW_ABSOLUTE_DIRECTORY --render`` for complete fresh inventories and targets. The explicitly named ``--reuse-recorded-boundaries`` mode acquires the exact complete target execution closures, then regenerates all inventories and all bounded controls. The original lambda4 deadline remains failed evidence only. The later root-symmetry deadline contributes only its individually returned calls through the accepted protocol.

The checker uses C++17 and 64-bit-word nauty. The canonical routine proposes literal maps, which are verified before any identification. PDFLaTeX and Ghostscript are needed for native rendering.
